#: content/en/posts/2023/krita-in-2022-and-2023.md:0
msgid "Krita in 2022 and 2023"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2023/krita-in-2022-and-2023.md:6
msgid ""
"This is our, very late, yearly overview of the year past, and look-forward "
"to the year that has just started. If that sort of thing bores you, feel "
"free to skip!"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2023/krita-in-2022-and-2023.md:8
msgid "![](images/posts/2023/electrichearts_20201224A_kiki_c1-1024x512.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2023/krita-in-2022-and-2023.md:10
msgid ""
"Like in 2021 and 2020, no members of the Krita team actually died from the "
"ongoing pandemic. This feels a bit miraculous, but there it is. The year was "
"pretty awful, though, with the Krita maintainer getting long COVID (that's "
"me, Halla...) and being too sick to do anything four days out of seven -- "
"and various other upheavals we're not going to detail because that would not "
"be safe, or would be too private to talk about, we really had a really tough "
"year."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2023/krita-in-2022-and-2023.md:12
msgid ""
"The years before 2022 were mostly marked by us trying, sometimes "
"desperately, to keep on top of the number of bug reports flowing in. A lot "
"of bug reports, it has to be said, are basically not actionable. That's not "
"to blame the reporter who went through the lengths needed to register and "
"then write up their problem. Which is really an admirable amount of effort. "
"But too often, the problems are with the OS support for tablets, display "
"drivers... And plain misunderstandings. And cries for user support. But "
"there are now more open bug reports than a year ago."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2023/krita-in-2022-and-2023.md:14
msgid "![](images/posts/2023/bugs_2022.png)"
msgstr "![](images/posts/2023/bugs_2022.png)"

#: content/en/posts/2023/krita-in-2022-and-2023.md:16
msgid ""
"So, for this year, we decided to take a different approach. We wanted to pro-"
"actively determine what _we_ wanted to work on, and then discuss how to do "
"that, and go for it, instead of just reacting to bug reports, wish bugs and "
"feature requests."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2023/krita-in-2022-and-2023.md:18
msgid ""
"So, early 2022, as soon as the lifting of lock-downs allowed, two Krita "
"developers, Halla and Wolthera, sat together in Deventer, to prepare this "
"idea. Of course, even before the invasion of Ukraine and all the problems "
"_that_ caused, we couldn't get a full Krita Developers' Sprint together. So, "
"this was limited."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2023/krita-in-2022-and-2023.md:20
msgid ""
"We sat down, the two of us, and discussed what Krita's main commercial "
"competition was. Well, that's Clip Studio, of course. Photoshop is not "
"really making progress when it comes to painting support, and Corel Painter "
"is not an application we would take as our example: we want to create the "
"most efficient application to create new images with. Turning photo's into "
"something painterly is not our goal."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2023/krita-in-2022-and-2023.md:22
msgid ""
"The result of that was a [document where we tried to identify the most "
"important things that were missing](https://docs.google.com/document/"
"d/18ZL_DiMc3VdtcN_dCz_BTMn1fR3M72GuRw2E4ThRdiw), or lacking, in Krita. This "
"is what we came up with:"
msgstr ""

